{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790974001,"nonce":"O09p3SqzywoIhAFDrRyqWbkiP7Y=","title":"A flow's print() writes to standard output","message":"Decided 2026-10-02 (Luis): print() in a flow goes to stdout, as in every language, so a flow that renders text (a report) prints its page and returns None; a returned value is still printed as JSON after it. Until now print() went to stderr so stdout stayed JSON for jq, which protected a composition nobody had used and left a text-rendering flow no way out. The runtime's own diagnostics (schema warnings) stay on stderr. Recorded in doc/design/config-entity.md.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["cli"],"priority":"medium","status":"done","type":"decision"}}]}